FindProof -- one binary, two roles: equational prover (CASC UEQ) and
first-order proof checker (ProoVer).

BUILD
  make                 # produces bin/FindProof  (needs a C11 compiler + libm)
  ./starexec_build     # equivalent, for StarExec

The whole engine is one self-contained translation unit; no external
dependencies beyond the C standard library and libm.

STAREXEC CONFIGURATIONS (both drive the same bin/FindProof)
  bin/starexec_run_default PROBLEM.p
      CASC UEQ proving.  Reads the wall-clock limit from
      $STAREXEC_WALLCLOCK_LIMIT (default 120s), runs a time-sliced
      portfolio, and writes an SZS status line plus, on success, an SZS
      CNFRefutation.
  bin/starexec_run_proover PROOF.p
      ProoVer proof checking.  Validates every derived step of a
      first-order TSTP proof and writes one SZS verdict
      (Verified / FailedVerified / NotVerified).  Wall-clock limit from
      $STAREXEC_WALLCLOCK_LIMIT (default 30s).

RUN (manual)
  bin/FindProof --schedule --szs --proof --wall=120 PROBLEM.p   # prove (CASC)
  bin/FindProof --szs PROBLEM.p                                 # prove, single config
  bin/FindProof --check --szs PROOF.p                           # check (ProoVer)
  bin/FindProof --list-knobs                                    # strategy surface

INPUT
  Proving  : TPTP CNF unit-equality problems.  include('Axioms/*.ax')
             directives resolve against the problem directory and $TPTP.
  Checking : first-order TSTP proofs (fof/cnf records with inference
             annotations), by refutation, closing with $false.
OUTPUT
  Proving  : SZS status (Unsatisfiable / Satisfiable / GaveUp /
             ResourceOut / Timeout) and, with --proof, a CNFRefutation.
  Checking : SZS verdict (Verified / FailedVerified / NotVerified); a
             localised faulty step is printed as a comment.
